      "problem": "Which of the following is a dodecahedron?",
      "worked_solution": "Among the given options, the *dodecahedron* is shown in the following picture:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14268510/assets/9775a0c005b7e5212654e4af71cf469c0522339141f228374d31d8aadfda5c8f.png)\n\nA dodecahedron is a regular polyhedron that \n\n- consists of $12$ congruent faces, each in the form of a regular pentagon, and\n\n- exactly $3$ faces meet at each vertex.\n\nRecall that there are only five types of Platonic solids (convex regular polyhedra):\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14268510/assets/bc67deabe1622e7ac3015c3ec942f254e59c58f406e026c367e0c0aeee5a6d3e.png)",
